{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what","id":209164,"title":"So...95% of the Novas are dead on my setting..Now what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-26T00:16:39-07:00","id":209164,"title":"So...95% of the Novas are dead on my setting..Now what?","content":"So, my players faced a villain from Adventure (a character i had when i was running that game) and this guy eficiently managed to <br /> A ) Uncover the existance of The Forbidden City<br /> B ) Managed to kill both Caesar Pax and Divis Mal<br /> C ) Detonated every single nuclear bomb on the Forbidden city while there was a warzone on the place with most of the Novas and managed to show humans that the novas are nothing more than bullies with superpowers.<br /> <br /> Now the public is afraid of novas, the directive doesnt know what to do, proyect utopia is pretty much torn a part, theres no team tomorrow, theres like 5 members left of the teragen and they are keeping low profile.<br /> <br /> any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T01:18:37-07:00","id":209191,"title":"","content":"It's maybe not the most productive thing, but an NPC did all that, despite the PCs working against him? It's your group/game, and as such I can't really judge what works and what doesn't, but if an ST I was playing under had that happen, I'd be feeling a bit pointless as a PC. Like it was more a &quot;look at this awesome character&quot; than a &quot;whee, we're superheroes!&quot;<br /> <br /> But putting that aside for the moment. If I were running the game, I'd let the PCs play the situation how they like. Work out the factions left, human and nova, but the PCs are going to want to do stuff. Support them in that, and emphasise their comparatively greater role in the world situation. Countries used to having novas around militarily, both as opponents and as soldiers, will have to adjust. Also bear in mind the advanced tech flow has dramatically reduced or stopped, and any catastrophic damage done during these events to the tech in question will be very difficult or impossible to repair for normal folks.<br /> <br /> Socially, people will regard novas with a greater degree of fear and hatred. It's not impossible they'll be attacked by people with weapons in large numbers, and any religious groups geared around hating novas will suddenly gain a large amount of support, if not actually believers. Governments <i>will</i> take notice of the PCs: whether that notice is hostile or recruit-y depends on the government, and may be a mix of both. Recruiters may start contacting the characters, and if they refuse, strike teams or outright missile strikes will follow after, very soon. Like, minutes.<br /> <br /> Anyone who was seen to associate with novas before will be socially shunned and stigmatised. Physical attacks are not out of the question. And given how central novas were previously, that'll have <i>serious</i> social ramifications, possibly devolving into outright civil war. Certainly gang-style violence.<br /> <br /> Has the character in question been killed/dealt with? He's going to be a major factor, and any government worth its salt will be trying to take him out. My guess, with a great deal of collateral damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:59:42-07:00","id":209308,"title":"","content":"Your players should now be some of the most powerful people on Earth. They could rebuild the factions they were part of, or start new ones. They are now the only ones left to do any and all good that was being done by Novas (assuming they are in anyway good guys). I'd probably let things spin out of control for a few sessions while they tried to hold things together and super-pulp guy slowly shows his true colors and takes over the world before the world realizes they've been played. Then I'd seed in some sort of method for Time-Travel (may be Max Mercer himself) and give the part a chance to travel back in time and stop the villain before he killed everyone and changed the world.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:40:45-07:00","id":212876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what#post209164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my players faced a villain from Adventure (a character i had when i was running that game) and this guy eficiently managed to<br /> A ) Uncover the existance of The Forbidden City<br /> B ) Managed to kill both Caesar Pax and Divis Mal<br /> C ) Detonated every single nuclear bomb on the Forbidden city while there was a warzone on the place with most of the Novas and managed to show humans that the novas are nothing more than bullies with superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this is the part that most amazes me - seriously, how does anyone get even <b>a tenth</b> of all Novas to be not only in the same place, but <b>fighting on the same side</b> considering their sheer degree of fractiousness on national, religious, philosophical, political, sexual, racial and who knows how many other lines they might make issue of?! That sounds as simple insanity without some humongous level of mass brainwashing - a whole different can of worms on itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what#post209164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the public is afraid of novas, the directive doesnt know what to do, project utopia is pretty much torn a part, theres no team tomorrow, theres like 5 members left of the teragen and they are keeping low profile.<br /> <br /> any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if &quot;95% of the Novas are dead&quot; is anything but hyperbole, the matter closed before it even started. The books have usually given us a &quot;1 Nova in a million people ratio&quot;, what would mean a 7 thousand Novas total in a world with about our current human population total. 5% of that means 350 Novas <b>in the whole world</b>. Add to that the fact a good fraction of those survivors might have been the &quot;combat worthless&quot; ones and &quot;dealing with the superpowered bullies&quot; sounds like far less of an issue than &quot;OMG, can we still keep all the crazy stuff they did to fix the enviroment/terraformation the planet working?! How do we take care of<b> the insane amount of fallout</b> caused by the demented psycho that thought <b>nuclear winter</b> (because that's basically what's going to take to kill thousands of novas in the same place with one blow) was a great way to save the world of superbeings???&quot;<br /> <br /> Whoever it was, that Inspired basically left the whole planet between a rock and a hard place and those remaining Novas as the closest thing to a stopgap solution, <b>if </b>people manage to collect the sense to see the world has gotten into <b>the brink of a extinction-level event</b> and <b>beggars can't be choosers</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-10-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T19:12:59-07:00","id":222677,"title":"","content":"When in doubt... Chromatics attack!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3453-nephandi","name":"Nephandi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:23:36-07:00","id":223248,"title":"","content":"Yeah, can't really argue against the inclusion of laser dinosaurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T03:50:52-07:00","id":226891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what?p=223248#post223248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, can't really argue against the inclusion of laser dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are <b>speaking </b>laser dinosaurs...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T06:58:36-07:00","id":226991,"title":"","content":"Or dinosaurs that shoot laser beams when they roar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T13:24:18-07:00","id":227287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what?p=226991#post226991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or dinosaurs that shoot laser beams when they roar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, those would be quite appropriate to a ground zero/burial place of hundreds to thousands of Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:57:58-08:00","id":300331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/209164-so-95-of-the-novas-are-dead-on-my-setting-now-what#post209164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my players faced a villain from Adventure (a character i had when i was running that game) and this guy eficiently managed to<br /> A ) Uncover the existance of The Forbidden City<br /> B ) Managed to kill both Caesar Pax and Divis Mal<br /> C ) Detonated every single nuclear bomb on the Forbidden city while there was a warzone on the place with most of the Novas and managed to show humans that the novas are nothing more than bullies with superpowers.<br /> <br /> Now the public is afraid of novas, the directive doesnt know what to do, proyect utopia is pretty much torn a part, theres no team tomorrow, theres like 5 members left of the teragen and they are keeping low profile.<br /> <br /> any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>well depending on the 'timeline' of this actually happening I would really find it hard to believe 'the plot device' was killed aka divis mal aka dr primoris. at the start of the 'aberrant' book (which is started by divis using quantum authority to boost humanity globally to 1 quantum causing the eruptions of those humans with the MR latent genome to erupt when stressed(note: the MR genome implies that they were latents which can become psiad, nova, or paramorph.) <br /> <br /> cross time travel is another way to deal with your villain, 'heroes' from an alternate timeline can arrive with foreknowledge of what has happened (prior to them leaving). AFAIK only paramorphs are resistant to being taken out by time travel, with the possible exception of novas who at any point became time travelers, therefore also being enabled to interfere.<br /> <br /> if your villain is a psion, they are weak vs novas. if your villain is a nova they are weak vs psions. if your villain is a paramorph/daredevil this would make things much more difficult but inspiration only goes so far, at most 15 inspiration (3 in each facet) only gives 30 inspiration pool, a true concerted effort would easily eliminate their pool of inspiration.<br /> <br /> if max mercer exists in your world remember he time travelled 200 years in the future and returned with that information. Aeon is prepared, and should not be so easily thwarted.<br /> <br /> most starting point novas a nuke is pretty laughable unless they are a complete patsy or egghead (read: mega social / mega mental focus). all it takes is ONE nova willing to sacrifice a bunch of health levels and or take 1 or 2 permanent taint to turn a lame power like bioluminescence into elemental mastery (nuclear) for just a single usage to negate them all. obviously this was very poorly thought out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4225-cowtankerous","name":"cowtankerous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:11:21-08:00","id":431519,"title":"","content":"Make like &quot;Post-Death/Rebirth of&quot; Superman. Rebuild. Get somebody on that fallout. Evacuate civvies.<br /> <br /> And if you can't do that, for whatever reason, find the bastard responsible and take him down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}